<title>HONG KONG: HK March orders on hand fall 11 pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK March orders on hand fall 11 pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department said March orders-on-hand fell 11 percent in value on the year against a revised 10 percent drop in February.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value of orders-on-hand in March 1997 over March 1996 (* means that comparative figure has been revised and *** means that the change is within +/- 0.5 percent):</p>
<p>						  March 1997  February 1997</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey  -11	    -10*</p>
<p> Wearing apparel				-4	     -5</p>
<p> Textiles					 -9	     -8</p>
<p>						  March 1997  February 1997</p>
<p> Electronic Products			 -16	    -15*</p>
<p> Electrical products			 -9	     -4</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		 -9	     +5*</p>
<p> Plastic products			    -17	    -21</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		   -1	     -2*</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
